{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RR2ckdfZrVEkoyKagWEb9b","type":"tool_result","content":"TALLY_BRIEF=/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/a1b421a2e0f360d65a99dd4392541ba5cea95defea30cf9bc525eea6bd24e6c5.json\n---\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task rdma-package: Close the RDMA package: the missing pin test plus the odinlink and kernel-truth folds. Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"host/rdma\\\",\\\"tests\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane. Definition of done, in this order: (1) run this task's acceptanceCriteria commands and see them pass; (2) `git add` every file you changed, within the write boundary stated above; (3) `git commit` on the branch already checked out in the assigned worktree; (4) run `git status --porcelain` and confirm it prints nothing before you exit. Ownership validation reads committed history only: an exit with uncommitted changes fails the attempt (\\\"agent left uncommitted changes; commit the task before ownership validation\\\") and the uncommitted work is discarded.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:45bac91db98960a263071888d9334031f3d858de5b15dff5c89024783e105111\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"bash -n host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh && grep -q '503c5ae1e72aa9ed91925dafa3d82ee2e992747f' host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh && grep -q '76ba39b630a70accb72f19388eefe48844b50eb8' host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh && ! grep -qE '^[[:space:]]*(sudo[[:space:]]+)?(insmod|modprobe)[[:space:]]' host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh && grep -qi 'physically present' host/rdma/attended-bringup.md && grep -qi 'worker first' host/rdma/attended-bringup.md && grep -qi 'deploy' host/rdma/attended-bringup.md && test -s host/rdma/ab-protocol.md\"],\"description\":\"Scripts syntax-clean, pins present, no auto-install, attended language present.\",\"id\":\"rdma-package-sound\"},{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"python3 -m unittest tests.test_rdma_package -v && grep -qi 'odinlink' host/rdma/ab-protocol.md && grep -q '7.2.2' host/rdma/attended-bringup.md && grep -qi 'wire-fallback' host/rdma/attended-bringup.md\"],\"description\":\"The pin test exists and passes; the odinlink fold, the 7.2.2 truth, and the wire-rung Gate 0 caveat landed in the docs.\",\"id\":\"rdma-pin-test\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"host/rdma\",\"tests\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"The two pin commits are asserted by the tests suite, not merely present in the script\",\"Tomorrow's attended bring-up doc tells the truth about kernel 7.2.2, the missing verbs devices, the wedge blast radius, and which transport rung a Gate 0 benchmark must carry\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"RE-SCOPED 2026-08-30 (second flow): the package files under host/rdma ALREADY EXIST on main and pass this lane's original acceptance argv verbatim — do NOT rewrite them wholesale, and do not end with an empty diff (the empty-diff completion failure is a known harness hazard). Concrete deliverables now: (1) tests/test_rdma_package.py — the test the original goal promised: assert both pin commits 503c5ae1e72aa9ed91925dafa3d82ee2e992747f and 76ba39b630a70accb72f19388eefe48844b50eb8 appear in host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh; assert no line of that script begins with insmod or modprobe (optionally sudo-prefixed) — the no-unattended-load invariant, spec F.1; assert host/rdma/attended-bringup.md carries the 'physically present' and 'worker first' language. (2) Fold the odinlink learnings (repo issue 6, evidence at the reference estate the issue names) into host/rdma/ab-protocol.md and host/rdma/attended-bringup.md as short dated appendix sections: terminal-failure framing for verbs init (on ANY init failure: no retry, restore the socket env byte-identical on both ranks, one restart, and the terminal fallback rung is ALWAYS the ethernet wire, never the second rail); the 11 microsecond one-way rail reference figure; the per-cable p2p ceiling asymmetry; and the measured hazard that a verbs transmit toward a closed peer receive ring stalls end-to-end credits and wedges the whole XDomain INCLUDING TCP on the same cable — recovery is reboot-only, which is why no verbs rung may ever appear in an unattended fallback ladder. (3) A dated 'state of tonight' preamble note in attended-bringup.md: no ibverbs device exists on either node right now, the staged module sets cover only kernels 7.1.4 and 7.2.0 while the fleet runs 7.2.2, so the attended morning fetch-and-build on BOTH nodes (running-kernel gate 7.2.2) precedes any A/B; the honest expectation from the one measured community precedent is about +3.4 percent over held TCP — adopt only on a fingerprint-clean counterbalanced majority win. The preamble must ALSO state the Gate 0 transport-rung caveat: the banked socket-transport benchmark that unlocks bring-up must have been measured over the Thunderbolt rail — a bench receipt whose transport record reads fn_transport_rung wire-fallback is a 5GbE artifact and does NOT satisfy Gate 0; on a wire-fallback night the attended morning first heals rail 0 and re-banks a rail-sockets bench before any verbs work. Keep every existing hard rule intact: nothing GPL vendored, nothing installs or loads automatically, one rail only, bring-up starts only after a committed socket-transport benchmark exists under results/. Boundaries: touch only host/rdma and tests/.\",\"id\":\"rdma-package\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/stage-weights.sh\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:fe9122567f61a3ff2f0fa2ba872e08f885158cdaa3d584270bd72b3302f22bbc\",\"title\":\"Close the RDMA package: the missing pin test plus the odinlink and kernel-truth folds\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"377ba269689b458c10903c86e579816d39478b34\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-6e234065e770/rdma-package\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"host/rdma\",\"tests\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/rdma-package-fe9122567f61a3ff\",\"taskId\":\"rdma-package\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/6e234065e770/rdma-package\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[],\"preparedCommentIds\":[],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":0,\"recheckedCursor\":0,\"registrationId\":\"01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ef1d37d-6f19-4b92-8ee7-3ab4af23febd","uuid":"15faec4d-0d67-483b-9f2f-cec7b5c7636f","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:46:09.741Z","tool_use_result"