{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018px8SZPHWBeL6TeRb6Upqn","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (413.9KB). Full output saved to: /home/tom/.claude/projects/-home-tom--local-state-tally-campaigns-flashnext-flashnext-6e234065e770-rdma-package/7ef1d37d-6f19-4b92-8ee7-3ab4af23febd/tool-results/bxc86gr8p.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\ndocs/GATE0.md:38:### Note on #6 — do not \"fix\" this fork-side\nhandoff/harvest-2026-08-29/capture/01a04c6d-4506-77d1-b081-bf5e49f60e16.host-tooling.out:431:{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"thinking_end\",\"contentIndex\":0,\"content\":\"This is a Tally spec-build task. We are responsible for the \\\"host-tooling\\\" task within the \\\"flashnext\\\" campaign. Important points:\\n\\n- Working directory: /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/57f87640bc5b/host-tooling — this is a git worktree of the flashnext repository.\\n- Task: Implement host/ tooling and scripts/run-tp2.sh according to spec sections #r4, #6.1 (the brief says 4.2, 4.3, 4.4, 4.5, 6.1), integrate the discipline of ds4-vllm-manifest.md §5 and dotfiles-observed.md §5, and additionally add tests/test_host_tooling.py.\\n- Write boundaries: only host/, scripts/run-tp2.sh, tests/.\\n- Acceptance criteria: bash -n against host/*.sh and scripts/run-tp2.sh. grep checks against fn-env.sh: PYTHONHASHSEED=0, NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME, thunderbolt0, NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1, VLLM_RAY_EXTRA_ENV_VAR_PREFIXES_TO_COPY=FN_. Unit flashnext-pair.service must have ExecStopPost and must not have WantedBy. Tests are python3 -m unittest tests.test_host_tooling -v.\\n- Guidance: Computed NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME. Unconditional NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1. Never export probe-read engine defaults. Receipts must match the schema in scripts/receipts-verify.py exactly. Worker-side actions via Ethernet 10.99.9.2. cluster-up is reap-then-gate.\\n- Commit the full result to the assigned branch tally-work/flashnext-57f87640bc5b/host-tooling (the branch of the workspace). Do not push or merge.\\n- Stateless reconcile: preserve the work already in the lane.\\n\\nFirst, investigate the worktree: git status, branch, existing files.\"}}\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ef1d37d-6f19-4b92-8ee7-3ab4af23febd","uuid":"26152f29-a899-4031-9a59-d17005e9773d","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:46:35.861Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"docs/GATE0.md:38:### Note on #6 — do not \"fix\" this fork-side\nhandoff/harvest-2026-08-29/capture/01a04c6d-4506-77d1-b081-bf5e49f60e16.host-tooling.out:431:{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"thinking_end\",\"contentIndex\":0,\"content\":\"This is a Tally spec-build task. We are responsible for the \\\"host-tooling\\\" task within the \\\"flashnext\\\" campaign. Important points:\\n\\n- Working directory: /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/57f87640bc5b/host-tooling — this is a git worktree of the flashnext repository.\\n- Task: Implement host/ tooling and scripts/run-tp2.sh according to spec sections #r4, #6.1 (the brief says 4.2, 4.3, 4.4, 4.5, 6.1), integrate the discipline of ds4-vllm-manifest.md §5 and dotfiles-observed.md §5, and additionally add tests/test_host_tooling.py.\\n- Write boundaries: only host/, scripts/run-tp2.sh, tests/.\\n- Acceptance criteria: bash -n against host/*.sh and scripts/run-tp2.sh. grep checks against fn-env.sh: PYTHONHASHSEED=0, NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME, thunderbolt0, NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1, VLLM_RAY_EXTRA_ENV_VAR_PREFIXES_TO_COPY=FN_. Unit flashnext-pair.service must have ExecStopPost and must not have WantedBy. Tests are python3 -m unittest tests.test_host_tooling -v.\\n- Guidance: Computed NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME. Unconditional NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1. Never export probe-read engine defaults. Receipts must match the schema in scripts/receipts-verify.py exactly. Worker-side actions via Ethernet 10.99.9.2. cluster-up is reap-then-gate.\\n- Commit the full result to the assigned branch tally-work/flashnext-57f87640bc5b/host-tooling (the branch of the workspace). Do not push or merge.\\n- Stateless reconcile: preserve the work already in the lane.\\n\\nFirst, investigate the worktree: git status, branch, existing files.\"}}\nhandoff/harvest-2026-08-29/capture/01a04c6d-4506-77d1-b081-bf5e49f60e16.host-tooling.out:435:{\"type\":\"message_end\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"This is a Tally spec-build task. We are responsible for the \\\"host-tooling\\\" task within the \\\"flashnext\\\" campaign. Important points:\\n\\n- Working directory: /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/57f87640bc5b/host-tooling — this is a git worktree of the flashnext repository.\\n- Task: Implement host/ tooling and scripts/run-tp2.sh according to spec sections #r4, #6.1 (the brief says 4.2, 4.3, 4.4, 4.5, 6.1), integrate the discipline of ds4-vllm-manifest.md §5 and dotfiles-observed.md §5, and additionally add tests/test_host_tooling.py.\\n- Write boundaries: only host/, scripts/run-tp2.sh, tests/.\\n- Acceptance criteria: bash -n against host/*.sh and scripts/run-tp2.sh. grep checks against fn-env.sh: PYTHONHASHSEED=0, NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME, thunderbolt0, NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1, VLLM_RAY_EXTRA_ENV_VAR_PREFIXES_TO_COPY=FN_. Unit flashnext-pair.service must have ExecStopPost and must not have WantedBy. Tests are python3 -m unittest tests.test_host_tooling -v.\\n- Guidance: Computed NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME. Unconditional NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1. Never export probe-read engine defaults. Receipts must match the schema in scripts/receipts-verify.py exactly. Worker-side actions via Ethernet 10.99.9.2. cluster-up is reap-then-gate.\\n- Commit the full result to the assigned branch tally-work/flashnext-57f87640bc5b/host-tooling (the branch of the workspace). Do not push or merge.\\n- Stateless reconcile: preserve the work already in the lane.\\n\\nFirst, investigate the worktree: gi