work already present in the assigned lane.\\\",\\\"campaign\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"flashnext\\\",\\\"repository\\\":\\\"mecattaf/flashnext\\\",\\\"issue\\\":{\\\"number\\\":\\\"1\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\\\"},\\\"runId\\\":\\\"sha256:fb730d179cda15553673d1ed775dfc6cd1f096cb8cdfb103615509462ce10794\\\"},\\\"task\\\":{\\\"acceptanceCriteria\\\":[{\\\"argv\\\":[\\\"bash\\\",\\\"-euc\\\",\\\"for f in host/*.sh scripts/run-tp2.sh; do bash -n \\\\\\\"$f\\\\\\\"; done && grep -q 'PYTHONHASHSEED=0' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'thunderbolt0' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'VLLM_RAY_EXTRA_ENV_VAR_PREFIXES_TO_COPY=FN_' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q 'ExecStopPost' host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service && ! grep -q 'WantedBy' host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service && python3 -m unittest tests.test_host_tooling -v\\\"],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Env doctrine present, units teardown-safe, all scripts syntax-clean, host tests pass.\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"host-doctrine\\\"}],\\\"conflictDomains\\\":[\\\"host\\\",\\\"scripts/run-tp2.sh\\\",\\\"tests\\\"],\\\"deliveredBehaviors\\\":[\\\"One command stands the pair service; one command tears it down; failure cannot strand ranks\\\",\\\"First light produces the four receipts the ladder grades\\\"],\\\"dependencies\\\":[],\\\"goal\\\":\\\"Write the host/ tooling and scripts/run-tp2.sh per spec claims 4.2, 4.3, 4.4, 4.5 and 6.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4, #r6), composing the disciplines in specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md section 5 and specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md section 5. host/fn-env.sh: PYTHONHASHSEED=0; PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True,garbage_collection_threshold:0.85; HSA_ENABLE_INTERRUPT=1; inductor and triton cache dirs under the state directory, never tmpfs; NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME set ONLY to the Thunderbolt rails that carry a routable /30 IP (rail 0 thunderbolt0/10.99.0.x is guaranteed; rail 1 thunderbolt1 is trained-but-IP-unconfigured today per dotfiles modules/lowlat-cluster.nix and MUST NOT be listed until it has a peer IP — a peerless link-local rail in the list hangs RCCL bootstrap; the env file computes this from `ip -br addr` at write time and logs which rails it chose, rather than hardcoding both); NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1 UNCONDITIONALLY (an ibverbs device now exists on the rails from the pre-arm bake; without this pin RCCL autodetects verbs and silently rides unproven RDMA — sockets are the transport of record until the attended morning A/B, evidence host/rdma/ab-protocol.md); VLLM_RAY_EXTRA_ENV_VAR_PREFIXES_TO_COPY=FN_; VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1; a loud comment forbidding exports of engine defaults read through is-set probes. host/fn-cluster-up.sh: podman on both nodes (worker over ssh on the wire), distributed head on the coordinator and worker join, worker python pool capped small, a hard two-GPU gate before serve, then the serve process at tensor-parallel size 2 with eager execution, model directory /var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8, served name flashnext; reap stranded serve processes before start and gate on zero residue. host/fn-cluster-down.sh: idempotent teardown both nodes. host/fn-preflight.sh: byte-diff of both ranks' FN_ env, latency-hold device read on both ends, per-rail link-speed record, round-trip probe on both rails. host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service: oneshot, RemainAfterExit, ExecStopPost teardown, no install section. scripts/run-tp2.sh: preflight, up, two greedy 300-token completions byte-compared, residency read after 50 warmed decode tokens (GTT per rank from sysfs plus process RSS plus table page-cache residency), fidelity capture (fixed-prompt losses and frontier logits under results/), then a 262144-context probe, writing receipts tp2.json, residency.json, fidelity.json, context.json per the receipts-verify.py schema. Extend tests/test_repo_invariants.py-adjacent coverage with tests/test_host_tooling.py asserting the env file carries the doctrine lines and unit files carry ExecStopPost and no WantedBy install. Boundaries: touch only host/, scripts/run-tp2.sh, and tests/.\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"host-tooling\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"implementation\\\",\\\"readFirst\\\":{\\\"specSections\\\":[\\\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4\\\",\\\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6\\\",\\\"specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md\\\",\\\"specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md\\\"],\\\"styleReferences\\\":[\\\"scripts/stage-weights.sh\\\",\\\"scripts/run-smoke.sh\\\"]},\\\"revision\\\":\\\"sha256:ab66c582012f053ffa092301faf6a9b042d52ad26c6baa1b6d149083241af99d\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Pair-service orchestration: env doctrine, cluster up/down, first-light runner\\\"},\\\"workspace\\\":{\\\"baseRev\\\":\\\"e4ac78a9ba2a84aca3baec47a4698602a2f3b850\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"tally-work/flashnext-57f87640bc5b/host-tooling\\\",\\\"conflictDomains\\\":[\\\"host\\\",\\\"scripts/run-tp2.sh\\\",\\\"tests\\\"],\\\"publishBranch\\\":\\\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/host-tooling-ab66c582012f053f\\\",\\\"taskId\\\":\\\"host-tooling\\\",\\\"worktreePath\\\":\\\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/57f87640bc5b/host-tooling\\\"},\\\"steering\\\":{\\\"channel\\\":\\\"locally-authorized-snapshot\\\",\\\"authorizedComments\\\":[{\\\"author\\\":\\\"uid:1000\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"PRE-DISPATCH STEER (overseer, arm-time — fold into your first brief). Semantic traps your grep gate cannot catch; all are hard requirements: (1) NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME must be COMPUTED from `ip -br addr` — only rails that actually carry a routable IP. Rail 1 (thunderbolt1) is trained but IP-UNCONFIGURED (169.254.x link-local, no peer): hardcoding both rails passes the grep and hangs RCCL bootstrap. In practice only thunderbolt0 (10.99.0.x /30) qualifies. (2) NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1 UNCONDITIONALLY in host/fn-env.sh — not conditional on device detection. ibverbs devices exist on BOTH nodes by design (usb4_rdma0 + usb4_rdma5); without the pin RCCL autodetects verbs and silently rides the unproven RDMA path. Sockets are the transport of record this run. (3) NEVER export a probe-read engine default: VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM, VLLM_MOE_USE_DEEP_GEMM, VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER* are read via is_set() probes — exporting the default diverts the oracle into a hard raise (spec F.9). (4) Receipts must match scripts/receipts-verify.py EXACTLY — run it against your own output before declaring done. (5) Worker-side actions ride the ethernet wire (10.99.9.2), never a 10.99.0.x Thunderbolt rail — rails carry tensors only. (6) cluster-up is reap-then-gate: reap stale processes first, then gate on health, in that order.\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-08-29T06:05:30.106Z\\\",\\\"id\\\":1,\\\"updatedAt\\\":\\\"2026-08-29T06:05:30.106Z\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"local://campaign/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering/1\\\"}],\\\"attemptReceipt\\\":{\\\"lateRecheckCommentIds\\\":[],\\\"preparedCommentIds\\\":[1],\\\"recheckTruncated\\\":false,\\\"rechecked\\\":true,\\\"source\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"local-jsonl\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering-v1.jsonl\\\",\\\"preparedCursor\\\":4,\\\"recheckedCursor\\\":4,\\\"registrationId\\\":\\\"01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae\\\"}},\\\"machineDiagnoses\\\":[],\\\"machineOutcomes\\\":[]}}\"}],\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1787988646298},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"This is a Tally spec-build task. We are responsible for the \\\"host-tooling\\\" task within the \\\"flashnext\\\" campaign. Important points:\\n\\n- Working directory: /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/57f87640bc5b/host-tooling — this is a git worktree of the flashnext repository.\\n- Task: Implement host/ tooling and scripts/run-tp2.sh according to spec sections #r4, #6.1 (the brief says 4.2, 4.3, 4.4, 4.5, 6.1), integrate the discipline of ds4-vllm-manifest.md §5 and dotfiles-observed.md §5, and additionally add tests/test_host_tooling.py.\\n- Write boundaries: only host/, scripts/run-tp2.sh, tests/.\\n- Acceptance criteria: bash -n against host/*.sh and scripts/run-tp2.sh. grep checks against fn-env.sh: PYTHONHASHSEED=0, NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME, thunderbolt0, NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1, VLLM_RAY_EXTRA_ENV_VAR_PREFIXES_TO_COPY=FN_. Unit flashnext-pair.service must have ExecStopPost and must not have WantedBy. Tests are python3 -m unittest tests.test_host_tooling -v.\\n- Guidance: Computed NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME. Unconditional NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1. Never export probe-read engine defaults. Receipts must match the schema in scripts/receipts-verify.py exactly. Worker-side actions via Ethernet 10.99.9.2. cluster-up is reap-then-gate.\\n- Commit the full result to the assigned branch tally-work/flashnext-57f87640bc5b/host-tooling (the branch of the workspace). Do not push or merge.\\n- Stateless reconcile: preserve the work already in the lane.\\n\\nFirst, investigate the worktree: git status, branch, existing files.\",\"thinkingSignature\":\"reasoning_content\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I have the brief. This is the **host-tooling** spec-build task for the `flashnext` campaign. Let me inspect the assigned worktree and lane first.\\n\\n\"},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_3a44eb8f55de4ee380025be2\",\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/57f87640bc5b/host-tooling && git status && git log --oneline -5 && git branch --show-current\"}},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_5180e2157bfa4c11aa6dcd11\",\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/57f87640bc5b/host-tooling && ls -la && find . -path ./.git -prune -o -type f -print | head -60\"}}],\"api\":\"openai-completions\",\"provider\":\"qwen-token-plan\",\"model\":\"qwen3.8-max\",\"usage\":{\"input\":2981,\"output\":633,\"cacheRead