{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYFZWESqZdDRnwybHdAg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TicHpTXTHiwaW4dXRoYTsS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nrdma-package: the pin test, plus the odinlink and kernel-truth folds\n\nThe package under host/rdma/ already existed and already passed its\noriginal acceptance argv; what was missing was the test that argv only\ndescribed, and the truth about what the fleet actually looks like tonight.\n\ntests/test_rdma_package.py asserts the package's invariants rather than\nits prose being merely present: both module pins (503c5ae core/net,\n76ba39b verbs provider) appear in fetch-and-build.sh and are full 40-hex\ncommits rather than the branch pin that let rdma-core drift in the\nreference estate; no line of that script starts a module load, bare or\nsudo-prefixed (spec F.1 -- staging and building is all it may do); and\nthe attended checklist still carries \"physically present\", \"worker\nfirst\", the 7.2.2 running-kernel gate, the wire-fallback Gate 0 caveat,\nthe single-rail contract, and the reboot-only wedge.\n\nattended-bringup.md gains a dated \"state of tonight\" preamble ahead of\nGate 0: /sys/class/infiniband is empty on both nodes, the staged module\nsets cover only 7.1.4/7.2.0 while the fleet runs 7.2.2, so the morning\nfetch-and-build on both nodes precedes any A/B; and a Gate 0 benchmark\nwhose fn_transport_rung reads wire-fallback is a 5GbE artifact that does\nnot unlock bring-up -- a wire night heals rail 0 and re-banks a\nrail-sockets bench first.\n\nBoth docs gain a dated odinlink appendix (repo issue 6): verbs init\nfailure is terminal -- no retry, byte-identical socket env restored on\nboth ranks, one restart, and the terminal rung is always the ethernet\nwire, never the second rail; the ~11 us one-way reference figure against\nthe +3.4% end-to-end delta it produces; the asymmetric per-cable p2p\nceiling (~20 Gb/s p2p on a 40 Gb/s link, 8.38 uni against 9.84 full\nduplex); and the wedge restated where the ladder is written, since a\nverbs transmit toward a closed peer RX ring takes TCP on the same cable\ndown with it and recovery is a reboot.\n\nEvery existing hard rule is intact: nothing GPL vendored, nothing loads\nautomatically, one rail only, no bring-up without a committed\nsocket-transport benchmark under results/.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit --no-pager log --oneline -1; git status --porcelain; echo \"[status empty above = clean]\"","description":"Commit on the assigned branch"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_read_input_tokens":111556,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":399},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ef1d37d-6f19-4b92-8ee7-3ab4af23febd","uuid":"54c819bd-ee99-4ac8-9fb0-3699c364ec80","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:50:32.657Z","request_id":"req_011CeYFZVNMFqL9tr4CHmmsr"}
