{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYFad6yF5uumTxQdku4N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Committed as `a7e523f` on `tally-work/flashnext-6e234065e770/rdma-package`; `git status --porcelain` prints nothing.\n\n**What landed** (307 insertions, no existing lines rewritten — the package files that already passed on main were appended to, not replaced):\n\n- **`tests/test_rdma_package.py`** (new) — 13 tests. Both pins (`503c5ae…`, `76ba39b…`) asserted present *and* asserted to be full 40-hex commits rather than branch tags (the drift mode the ds4 manifest records for rdma-core); `bash -n` on the script; the no-unattended-load invariant as a line-anchored regex mirroring the acceptance argv (spec F.1); and the doc-truth assertions — `physically present`, `worker first`, `7.2.2`, `wire-fallback`, Gate 0's `results/` requirement, the single-rail contract, the odinlink fold in both docs, and `reboot-only`.\n- **`host/rdma/attended-bringup.md`** — dated \"State of tonight\" preamble ahead of Gate 0 (empty `/sys/class/infiniband` on both nodes; staged sets cover 7.1.4/7.2.0 against a 7.2.2 fleet, so the morning fetch-and-build on both nodes gates the A/B; the `fn_transport_rung: wire-fallback` caveat with the asymmetric dark-rail branch; the honest +3.4% expectation), plus Appendix A with the odinlink fold.\n- **`host/rdma/ab-protocol.md`** — dated odinlink appendix: the ~11 µs one-way figure against the +3.4% end-to-end delta it yields, the per-cable p2p ceiling asymmetry (~20 Gb/s p2p on a 40 Gb/s link; 8.38 uni vs 9.84 full-duplex), and the terminal-failure framing for verbs init.\n\n**Verification:** both acceptance argv run verbatim, exit 0. Full suite — all six test modules, 67 tests — passes, which includes `test_repo_invariants`'s no-GPL-text and script-syntax sweeps over the files I touched.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the brief names \"repo issue 6, evidence at the reference estate the issue names,\" and no issue-6 text exists in this worktree. I sourced the figures from the operator's local reference estate instead (`~/trans.md:532` for the 11 µs one-way and the 22 µs/286 µs and 8.38/9.84 Gb/s table, `~/additional-research.md:330,388` for the +3.4% A/B and OdinLink's documented two-cable breakage, `docs/DECISIONS-2026-08-30.md` §2.1/§2.4/§8.5 for the 7.2.2 truth, the wedge, and the asymmetric dark rail). Every number in the appendices traces to one of those; none is invented."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1022,"cache_read_input_tokens":111955,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1022},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ef1d37d-6f19-4b92-8ee7-3ab4af23febd","uuid":"007ea349-109e-4520-9c9a-8854911d66eb","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:50:47.434Z","request_id":"req_011CeYFacG7eF2jzKAN3ZYnx"}
